# TerraTone — Details: Features, Libraries & Simulations

TerraTone ("Hear the Pulse of Our Planet") is an offline-capable Earth-science sonification PWA:
pick a dataset (bundled demo, live NASA data, or your own CSV/JSON), watch it as a chart, and hear it
as synchronized sound. It also ships a Tornado Simulator and a library of nine more 3D hazard-training
worlds, each with its own procedural audio engine.

Everything runs in the browser. No account, no paid API, no backend. All simulated values and sounds
are labeled as simulated; AI output is labeled as AI; nothing pretends to be a real recording or forecast.

---

## 1. Features (detailed)

### 1.1 Explore (dashboard)
- Logo + connection badge: Online / Offline / Using cached data.
- Featured datasets, search box, category filters (only populated categories shown).
- Recently played list, "how it works" explainer, per-dataset source attribution.

### 1.2 Listen (visualization + sonification)
- Canvas time-series chart: playhead, legend, units, color scale, missing-data bands, timeline
  scrubber, speed control, transports (play / pause / resume / restart / stop), date labels.
- Web Audio sonification engine, deterministic mappings:
  - value -> pitch on a log scale,
  - magnitude -> safe loudness band (compressor-capped),
  - precipitation-style note density,
  - longitude -> stereo pan, time -> note sequence.
- 4 sound profiles: Musical (pentatonic), Ambient (slow pads), Minimal (short sine blips),
  Scientific (unquantized linear pitch + data ticks).
- Master volume, mute, tone preview, audio-only mode, user-gesture audio unlock, clean node teardown.
- Accessibility companions: captions log per frame, text data summary.
- Optional "Explain this" via Gemini, always labeled AI-generated, never NASA data; answers can be read
  aloud with the browser's built-in voice (voice on/off persisted, explicit read/stop, works offline once
  generated).

### 1.3 Live hub (online)
- NASA EONET natural-events feed (keyless): category filters, interactive Leaflet events map,
  IndexedDB-cached copies for offline viewing.
- One-tap launch from a live wildfire / volcano / storm / quake event into the matching simulator.
- NASA EPIC live Earth photos and APOD space bonus (uses your key or the shared DEMO_KEY).

### 1.4 Tornado Simulator (launched from the Sims tab)
- Real-time Three.js world in a lazy-loaded chunk (zero impact on the main bundle).
- Controllable astronaut-like explorer: third-person camera; WASD/arrows + Shift + Space + Esc on
  desktop; joystick + drag-camera + walk/run toggle + optional gyro on mobile.
- Rotating funnel with debris/wind particles, tumbling wreckage orbiting it, funnel-lift that picks
  the explorer off the ground up close.
- Roaming funnel with a yellow catch ring: cross it to get picked up, struggle out, or get flung clear.
- Trees flattened in its path; scattered bystanders recover after being hit.
- Rideable helicopter (hold Run to climb) and car parked by spawn — board with E; both are large and
  visible across the map, both snatchable by the funnel.
- Bystanders steal parked vehicles for joyrides (the funnel grabs those too).
- Storm clouds, lightning, terrain/roads/trees/buildings with collision, wandering MC-style NPC
  bystanders, distance rings.
- Fully procedural Web Audio storm engine (synthesized only, never a real recording): rumble + wind +
  whistle + gusts + thunder + debris, driven continuously by character->funnel distance via a smooth
  non-linear curve; PannerNode spatial audio with stereo fallback; limiter-capped output.
- 5 presets (Distant -> Extreme + Custom), live waveform/spectrum from an AnalyserNode, per-layer
  mixer, Low/Med/High graphics, pause/resume/reset/mute, educational disclaimer.
- Works offline after first load (service worker caches `/assets/` chunks).

### 1.5 Simulator Library (Sims tab)
- The Tornado Simulator (dedicated engine, section 1.4 + 3.2) plus nine training worlds on a shared
  engine (generic EnvSim 3D world + AmbienceEngine procedural audio
+ pure per-hazard mappings), each with its own environment, sound design, and parameters — full breakdown
in section 3. (Upgrade in progress: the 10 planned worlds in `PLAN.md` — flash flood, landslide and
drought have shipped.)
Every sim card shows its own hand-drawn procedural SVG scene (inline `SimArt` — offline, no image files,
screen-reader labeled) using the sim's accent palette. Category cards, difficulty badges, presets, launch buttons; all values labeled simulated,
with safety guidance and offline replay.

### 1.6 Earth Jukebox Studio
- Pipeline: dataset -> range -> mapping -> preview -> synced play -> save preset -> export/share JSON.
- Optional clip recording via MediaRecorder (compatibility notes shown; `audio/webm;codecs=opus` preferred).
- Time-range applies to saved presets/exports; live playback uses the full series.

### 1.7 3D music view (Listen / Studio player)
- Lazy three.js **data landscape** (`components/MusicViz3D.tsx`) with bloom post-processing (EffectComposer +
  UnrealBloomPass + OutputPass): one column per sampled frame along the time axis — up to 150 columns,
  evenly subsampled for long records with an honest on-screen note ("1 column ≈ N frames"). Column height
  and color encode the value on a semantic ramp chosen per dataset family: temperature → blue–white–red
  diverging *centered at zero* for signed anomalies; sea level / tides / sea ice / glacier / ocean and
  precipitation → deep blue → aqua; fires / storm winds / lightning / urban heat → dark gold → hot red;
  vegetation / CO₂ → dim → bright green; sun & space weather → indigo → magenta.
- Playhead: the played column pulses (with RMS + note accents), a floor ring, beacon sphere, light column
  and a floating canvas label ("time · value · units", "no data" for gaps) track it. Each scheduled note
  fires a spinning shard from the playhead column top (x offset = stereo pan) via the engine `onNote` bus.
- Master-bus level: the post-master `AnalyserNode` RMS gently pumps bloom strength, the playhead pulse
  and beacon scale (idle mode is labeled in the overlay).
- Atmosphere: glow backdrop, starfield, grid, fog. Camera: drag to orbit (damped), follows the playhead
  while playing (smooth x-track), slow cinematic orbit of the whole record when idle; reduce-motion
  disables the idle auto-orbit. On-screen legend shows the ramp gradient, min/max + units.
- WebGL failure falls back to "WebGL unavailable" with chart + captions intact; pixel ratio capped;
  dispose-safe on unmount; toggleable ("🧊 3D music view") and hidden in audio-only mode. Ships as a
  ~10 KB gzip lazy chunk (includes the bloom passes).

### 1.8 Library (datasets)
- 17 bundled synthetic demos installed on first launch (temperature, CO₂, sea level, monsoon, fires,
  vegetation, tides, sunspots, seismic, sea ice, lightning, Kp, aurora, urban heat, coral, cyclone wind, glacier).
- Every dataset card (Explore featured + Library) shows a category-tinted sparkline thumbnail of its real
  values (`components/DataArt.tsx`, inline SVG, offline, demo-labeled).
- Search / filter / sort; states downloaded / pending / failed / cancelled; offline badges.
- CSV + JSON import with validation (512 KB / 5,000-point caps) and row-level error reporting.
- Download with progress + cancel, delete, storage usage, interrupted-download tolerance,
  clear "cannot fetch live data offline" messaging.

### 1.9 Talking NPCs (every simulator)
- Walk up to any named bystander and press T (or the Talk button).
- Speech bubble floats at the NPC's head (tail pointing down at them); quick questions and your input
  dock to the bottom of the view.
- NPC stops and turns to face you while chatting.
- Answers are read aloud with the browser's built-in voice (SpeechSynthesis): toggle persisted,
  click any reply to replay.
- Answers come through your Gemini key, grounded in NASA research notes plus live sim state, with real
  NASA source links and honest AI labeling.

### 1.10 Character editor
- Headgear (helmet/cap/bare), 3 visors + tints, 3 faces, 4 hairstyles, 5 skin tones, 6 suits +
  6 accents, 3 builds; presets + randomize; live spinning 3D preview.
- Applied instantly in every simulator, saved on-device; every NPC bystander gets its own randomized
  look from the same system. Lives on the Settings page.

### 1.11 Minimap
- Live minimap of each sim with hazard / NPC / vehicle blips and labels, heading, distance/bearing
  chips, and culling for off-view events.

### 1.12 Controls & keyboard
- Desktop: WASD/arrows, Shift (run), Space (jump; climb while riding the sub), Esc (release pointer),
  E (board/exit vehicles), T (talk to nearby NPC).
- Mobile: virtual joystick, drag camera, walk/run toggle, optional gyro.
- Inputs are ignored while typing in chat; releasing keys stops movement immediately; window blur
  failsafe clears stuck keys.

### 1.13 Offline / PWA
- `manifest.webmanifest` + hand-rolled service worker (`public/sw.js`): app-shell + data caches,
  `/assets/` chunks cached for sims.
- IndexedDB (`terratone`): datasets, experiences, settings, EONET cache.
- Bundled synthetic demos installed on first launch; installable on Android (HTTPS required),
  Add to Home Screen on iOS.

### 1.14 Accessibility (Access tab)
- Semantic HTML, skip link, keyboard map, visible focus, high-contrast theme, 4 text sizes,
  reduce-motion, quiet mode, color-independent status badges.
- Honest framing throughout: "sound is a companion, not a conclusion."

### 1.15 Settings
- Default sound profile, volume, reduce-motion and related preferences.
- Character editor (AvatarStudio).
- API keys entry was removed (Oct 2026); keys now come from `frontend/.env` at build time only.

### 1.16 Optional keyed extras (online only)
- NASA EPIC live Earth photos and APOD in the Live tab (your key, else shared DEMO_KEY).
- Gemini explanations of any sonification on Listen and NPC chat answers — always labeled AI-generated;
  both can be read aloud with the browser's built-in voice.
- Keys live in `frontend/.env` (`VITE_NASA_API_KEY`, `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY`, git-ignored, never committed;
  see `.env.example`). Rebuild after editing `.env` (values bake in at build time).

### 1.17 Tests
- 137 Vitest unit tests across 15 files (normalization, missing/outlier handling, audio bounds,
  import/export, timeline sync, storm distance curve, level mapping, bearings, movement/collision,
  presets, hazard audio mappings, tremor/drift/HUD, EPIC URL builder, Gemini helpers, on-device key
  storage, error-boundary recovery, EONET geometry/mapping/filtering, APOD parsing, per-sim tick modes,
  sub-bass curves, saturation curve, avatar profiles/persistence/builder, ocean depth gauge, NASA guide
  knowledge, NPC names, notice/emote behavior, flash-flood water-level model, slope-stability + reservoir-balance models,
  sim illustrations, dataset-sparkline art,
  bundled-demo integrity + range honesty, data-landscape layout and
  semantic ramps, AI-voice speech cleanup) — all passing.
  Run: `npx vitest run`.

### 1.18 Realistic procedural audio (shared)
- Breathing sine sub-bass under every rumble (`attachSubBass`), gentle saturation glue (`softClipCurve`),
  two-stage thunder (close crack + rolling tail with re-strike via `thunderStrike`), resonant
  fire/debris pops, rain patter that follows the rainfall slider, pitch-dropping bubble bloops underwater.
- All synthesized locally, all limiter-capped for safe output.

