## 3. Simulations (detailed)

### 3.1 Shared engine (all 9 hazard sims)
- `EnvSim`: Three.js world with terrain, roads, trees/buildings, colliders; player controller
  (walk/run/jump, vehicles); NPC bystanders (2–6 by quality tier, toggleable) that flee the hazard
  and notice the visitor — within ~24 m they may pause, turn toward you and pop a weighted random
  emote bubble (👋 😄 👍 ❗ ❤️, sprite above the head, deterministic per seed, 18–44 s cooldown,
  cancelled while fleeing or chatting);
  hazard vector = distance + bearing from the hazard point to the player (audio, HUD, NPC threat,
  minimap all use the same source).
- `AmbienceEngine`: procedural noise-layer audio (each hazard defines its own layer set below),
  smooth non-linear distance->intensity curve, limiter-capped output, per-layer mixer.
- Each hazard is a pure `HazardDef` (parameters, presets, gains, HUD, gauges, safety copy) plus a
  `Feature(ctx)` pack that builds its distinct environment.
- Shared UI: launch cards with category/difficulty/presets, parameter sliders, audio mixer +
  waveform/spectrum, minimap, pause/reset, HUD chips, safety note, "simulated" labels everywhere.
  Every card shows a procedural SVG scene (`components/SimArt.tsx`) matching the sim's accent palette.

### 3.2 Tornado Simulator
- Category: Storms & wind. Dedicated engine (`TornadoScene` + `stormEngine`), not EnvSim.
- Parameters (Custom preset): intensity, wind speed (Km/h sim), wind volume, rumble depth, gust rate,
  distance.
- Presets: Distant Storm (0.15 / 40 km/h / dist 320), Developing Tornado (0.4 / 110 / 220),
  Strong Tornado (0.7 / 180 / 150), Extreme Tornado (1 / 260 / 110, audio stays capped), Custom.
- Environment/interactions: rotating funnel, debris + wind particles, tumbling wreckage, yellow catch
  ring (pickup / struggle out / flung clear), funnel-lift, flattened trees, recovering bystanders,
  rideable helicopter (climb with Run) and car (board with E), NPC vehicle joyrides, storm clouds,
  lightning, distance rings.
- Audio layers: rumble, wind, whistle, gusts, thunder, debris — spatially panned (PannerNode with
  stereo fallback), driven by distance curve; analyser waveform/spectrum; per-layer mixer.

### 3.3 Hurricane Simulator
- Category: Storms & wind. Difficulty: Intense. Spawn: 280/190/130 m from the eye.
- A **drifting eye** that wanders: speed scales with intensity (1.5 + intensity * 4.5 m/s), steers
  back when farther than 80 m from origin, clamped to a ±70 m box; distance, audio, NPC threat,
  bearings, and the minimap all follow it.
- Parameters: storm intensity (0.1–1), rainfall rate (0–1), wind speed (60–280 km/h sim),
  storm direction (0–360°).
- Presets: Tropical Storm (0.3 / 0.4 / 90 / 40), Major Hurricane (0.7 / 0.7 / 190 / 40),
  Extreme Landfall (1 / 1 / 270 / 40).
- Environment: eyewall, rain bands, surf, storm direction, thrashing palms, flying debris, foam rings.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 80 Hz), wind (white band-pass 500 Hz), rain (white high-pass
  4.5 kHz), surf (brown low-pass 220 Hz).
- HUD: wind (sim), rain (sim), eye distance, eye bearing. Safety: never chase real hurricanes.

### 3.4 Earthquake Simulator
- Category: Geology. Difficulty: Moderate. Spawn: 150 m from epicenter (all presets).
- Parameters: magnitude (3–8.5 Mw sim), tremor duration (5–60 s), camera shake (0–1).
- Presets: Minor Tremor (4 / 10 s / 0.5), Major Quake (6.5 / 25 / 0.8), Great Quake (8.2 / 45 / 1).
- Environment: triggered tremors (button), camera shake, live seismograph drawing P/S/coda phases,
  swaying lamps, falling rubble, sparking power lines.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 60 Hz), grind (white band-pass 240 Hz), creak (white band-pass
  900 Hz, high resonance).
- HUD: magnitude, shaking %, epicenter distance, duration. Safety: Drop, Cover, and Hold On.

### 3.5 Volcano Simulator
- Category: Geology. Difficulty: Intense. Spawn: 220/170/140 m from crater.
- Parameters: eruption intensity (0.05–1), ash emission (0–1), lava output (0–1).
- Presets: Strombolian Bursts (0.35 / 0.3 / 0.6), Vulcanian Column (0.65 / 0.7 / 0.4),
  Plinian Blast (1 / 1 / 0.7).
- Environment: slope-hugging lava flows, churning crater lava lake, ballistic bombs, ash column with
  fallout, steaming fumaroles, gas bursts, solid crater.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 70 Hz), roar (white band-pass 350 Hz), ash wind (1400 Hz),
  hiss (high-pass 5.2 kHz).
- HUD: eruption, ash, crater distance, crater bearing. Safety: pyroclastic flows kill from kilometers away.

### 3.6 Deep Ocean Simulator
- Category: Oceans. Difficulty: Gentle. Spawn: 120 m (all presets).
- Parameters: depth (5–200 m), current strength (0–1), water temperature (−2–30 °C).
- Presets: Sunlit Reef (12 m / 0.25 / 24 °C), Twilight Zone (120 / 0.55 / 8), Abyss Edge (195 / 0.3 / 2).
- Environment: diver, bubbles (pitch-dropping bloops), whale tone, current drift, rideable scuba sub,
  fish schools, patrolling sharks, pulsing jellyfish, a passing whale, marine snow, seagrass.
- Audio layers: wash (brown low-pass 300 Hz), flow (white band-pass 700 Hz), sparkle (high-pass 6 kHz),
  geo (brown low-pass 55 Hz — geological groans at depth).
- HUD: depth, current, temperature, light zone + **depth gauge** (~m / ~atm / zone).

### 3.7 Wildfire Simulator
- Category: Land & forests. Difficulty: Intense. Spawn: 200/160/130 m from the front.
- Parameters: fire intensity (0.05–1), vegetation dryness (0–1), wind speed (0–60 km/h sim),
  wind direction (0–360°).
- Presets: Smoldering Edge (0.25 / 0.4 / 8 / 90), Crown Run (0.7 / 0.8 / 30 / 90),
  Megafire Blowup (1 / 1 / 55 / 90).
- Environment: flame front, smoke and embers, arcing firebrands, glowing ground embers, fleeing deer.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 110 Hz), roar (white band-pass 420 Hz), wind (800 Hz).
- HUD: front intensity, dryness, fireline distance, wind speed + direction.
  Safety: leave early, never outrun a front.

### 3.8 Tsunami Simulator
- Category: Oceans. Difficulty: Intense. Spawn: 240/170/120 m from the front.
- Parameters: wave height (2–20 m), wave speed (30–120 km/h sim), surge run-up (0–1),
  sea temperature (−2–30 °C).
- Presets: Distant Swell (4 m / 40 / 0.3 / 20 °C), Coastal Warning (10 / 75 / 0.55 / 17),
  Mega Tsunami (20 / 115 / 0.8 / 15).
- Environment: advancing wave front with inland surge, spray, floating debris, stilt houses.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 55 Hz), surge (brown low-pass 160 Hz), rush (white band-pass
  420 Hz), spray (high-pass 5.5 kHz).
- HUD: wave height, wave speed, front distance, ETA + **wave-energy gauge** (height % / speed %).
  Safety: strong/long shaking or the sea pulling back means go to high ground immediately.

### 3.9 Flash Flood Simulator
- Category: Water & floods. Difficulty: Moderate. Spawn: 140/120/100 m from the river gauge.
- Illustrative model (`floodLevel`): rainfall × soil intake -> runoff, retention by drainage,
  relief concentrates the peak; returns a simulated water level 0..1 (unit-tested, bounded).
- Parameters: rainfall rate (0–120 mm/h sim), soil intake (0–1), drainage capacity (0–1),
  terrain relief (0–1).
- Presets: Urban Downpour (45 / 0.6 / 0.8 / 0.35), Monsoon Deluge (85 / 0.35 / 0.4 / 0.55),
  Cloudburst Catastrophe (120 / 0.15 / 0.15 / 0.7).
- Environment: canal between two levees, overflow sheet across the town as the level tops the
  north levee, rain curtain + low cloud deck, runoff cascades off terraced hills (scale with the
  relief slider), storm-drain grates, depth markers, floating debris, river gauge staff.
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 90 Hz), rain (white high-pass 3.8 kHz),
  runoff (white band-pass 600 Hz), surge (brown low-pass 180 Hz); hiss ticks track rainfall.
- HUD: rainfall (sim), runoff %, gauge distance, flood stage; **flood gauge** meter (depth in m,
  normal / rising / flooding). Safety: never drive through flooded roads; most deaths are in vehicles.

### 3.10 Landslide Simulator
- Category: Geology. Difficulty: Moderate. Spawn: 160/130/100 m from the slide scar.
- Illustrative model (`slopeStability`): slope angle sets the driving stress, soil saturation +
  rainfall raise pore-water pressure (lowering friction), vegetation root cohesion resists; returns a
  0..1 stability index (unit-tested, bounded, monotonic in each input).
- Parameters: slope angle (5–60° sim), soil saturation (0–1), rainfall rate (0–120 mm/h sim),
  vegetation cover (0–1).
- Presets: Rooted Slope (18 / 0.3 / 20 / 0.9), Saturated Watch (38 / 0.7 / 70 / 0.4),
  Slope Failure (55 / 0.95 / 110 / 0.1).
- Environment: terraced hillside rising north, dark scarp face, crest cracks that open with
  instability, debris tongue creeping downhill (worst when saturated), boulders that start rolling
  when the slope gives, vegetation tinted by the cover slider, rain curtain, scarp dust puffs,
  survey staff at the scar (minimap event anchor).
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 70 Hz), crack (white band-pass 1.5 kHz, Q 6),
  debris (white band-pass 700 Hz), rain (white high-pass 4.2 kHz); pop ticks track crack density.
- HUD: stability index, saturation, slope, scarp distance; **slope stability** meter
  (stable / watch / failure likely). Safety: in real terrain watch for fresh cracks, leaning trees
  and sudden springs after heavy rain, and evacuate early.

### 3.11 Drought Simulator
- Category: Water & climate. Difficulty: Moderate. Spawn: 150/120/100 m from the reservoir.
- Illustrative model (`reservoirLevel`): rainfall in vs evaporation + demand out, buffered by
  reservoir capacity; returns stored fraction 0..1 (unit-tested, bounded, monotonic in each input).
- Parameters: monthly rainfall (0–150 mm/mo sim), evaporation (0–1), crop & city demand (0–1),
  reservoir capacity (0.2–1).
- Presets: Wet Season (120 / 0.3 / 0.4 / 0.8), Dry Spell (45 / 0.55 / 0.7 / 0.6),
  Mega-Drought (5 / 0.9 / 0.95 / 0.35).
- Environment: reservoir basin with clay rim, water disc that shrinks and drops with the modeled
  level, historic shoreline bands, radial mud cracks + pits revealed on the drying bed, crop field
  fading green → straw, dust streaming leeward with evaporation strength, rim houses (colliders),
  monitoring pole at the rim (minimap event anchor).
- Audio layers: rumble (brown low-pass 80 Hz), wind (white band-pass 550 Hz),
  dust (white high-pass 5.2 kHz); pop ticks model cracking mud; hollow tone descends as the level falls.
- HUD: reservoir %, rainfall, evaporation, shoreline distance; **reservoir level** meter
  (comfortable / dropping / critical). Safety: real droughts bring rationing, crop losses, heat waves
  and wildfire risk — conserve water before a crisis is declared.

### 3.12 NPCs, guides & provenance in sims
- Every sim has named NPC bystanders that wander, flee the hazard, stop and face you while chatting,
  and answer grounded questions (guide topics cover all 10 sims: tornado, hurricane, earthquake,
  volcano, ocean, tsunami, wildfire, flood, landslide, drought).
- All simulated values are labeled "(sim)"; all sounds are synthesized; disclaimers state the sims are
  learning toys, not forecasts or survival training.

---

## 4. Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Dev server at http://localhost:5173 |
| `npm run build` | Typecheck (`tsc --noEmit`) + production build to `dist/` |
| `npm run preview` | Serve the production build (port 4173) |
| `npm test` | Run the 95 unit tests once (`vitest run`) |
